## Project Overview
This is a static personal website for deanlyoung.com. It uses:
- Plain HTML/CSS/JS (no framework)
- Markdown blog system with a custom `build.js` (Node.js)
- GitHub Pages for deployment

## Local Development Server
- **Always preview via localhost** — never open HTML files directly with `open <file>.html`
- Use `npm run serve` to start the local server (uses `serve.sh` which checks for port conflicts)
- The site is served from the project root at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`
- To open a page in the browser: `open http://127.0.0.1:8000/<page>/`
  - Example: `open http://127.0.0.1:8000/philosophy/`
  - Example: `open http://127.0.0.1:8000/about/`
- If blog content has changed, run `npm run build` before serving
- `serve.sh` checks if port 8000 is already in use — if so, it prints a message and exits gracefully instead of crashing

## npm Scripts
- `npm run build` — builds blog posts from markdown to HTML (warns about unreviewed posts, does not block)
- `npm run review` — checks all posts against the editorial standard; exits non-zero on failure
- `npm run serve` — starts `live-server` on port 8000 (via `serve.sh`, with port conflict detection)
- `npm start` — builds blog posts then starts the server

## Editorial Standard
Every blog post must pass editorial review before publishing. The standard is defined in `EDITORIAL-STANDARD.md`.

- Each post's frontmatter must include an `editorial_review` block with seven criteria, all set to `true`
- `npm run review` validates all posts — CI runs this before build and blocks deployment on failure
- `npm run build` prints non-blocking warnings for unreviewed posts (allows local preview of drafts)
- When creating or editing a blog post, always include the `editorial_review` frontmatter block
- The seven criteria: `personally_specific`, `intellectually_honest`, `generous_to_subjects`, `observation_separated_from_fact`, `date_bound_advice_dated`, `opinions_earned`, `rights_cleared`
- `npm run review` also checks markdown formatting: frontmatter fields, reference links, footnotes, heading hierarchy, image alt text, trailing whitespace, and empty content

## File Structure
- `index.html` — homepage
- `about/index.html` — about page
- `philosophy/index.html` — philosophy page
- `craft/index.html` — craft page
- `resume/index.html` — resume page
- `blog/index.html` — blog listing (generated)
- `content/blog/*.md` — blog post source files (markdown)
- `css/styles.css` — all site styles
- `js/scripts.js` — all site JavaScript
- `build.js` — blog build script
- `review.js` — editorial review checker script
- `EDITORIAL-STANDARD.md` — editorial standard definition and workflow
- `assets/` — images, icons, and static files

## Coding Conventions
- Use the existing CSS variables in `:root` (e.g., `--ink`, `--warm-paper`, `--oxblood`, `--deep-moss`, `--golden-ochre`)
- Follow the existing HTML structure pattern: `.site-shell` > `.site-header` + `main.content.page-content` + `.site-footer`
- Keep JS in `js/scripts.js` — no inline scripts except analytics/JSON-LD
- All pages include JSON-LD structured data in the `<head>`